  "description": "IQAHIU crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R 3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H99 Cd3 N6 O27 Yb3,3(C4 H10 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 10 O neighbors; Cd1 (Cd) has 4 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 10 O neighbors; Cd2 (Cd) has 4 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 10 O neighbors; Cd3 (Cd) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.784-4.987 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.54-172.59°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C132H129N6O32Cd3Yb3. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
